# Line endings are normalized to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, git on Windows checks text files out with CRLF by default, and
# the tests compare text the repository holds: the worked examples of MFH Studio
# (src/studio/library) must be, byte for byte, what the code generation writes
# from their own models, and that comparison is one stray `\r` away from a
# failure that says nothing about the code.
#
# LF everywhere also keeps a diff from showing every line of a file as changed
# the first time a Windows contributor saves it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, left exactly as they are.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
